Being burdened is *not* excusable, even for a wizard. One might say,
especially for an (early) wizard, since they often need to *run*. Exercise
your strength, stash away your spellbooks and other stuff you don't need with
you. If you're always near the threshold, stash more often. Put everything in
the stash except your armor, weapon, some food and your emergency items. Come
back to the stash if you need something special, carefully move the stash when
the way gets too long.

You definitely don't need 40 daggers. Daggers are a little heavy, and 40 of
them weigh way too much for almost any character. Half of that is still
plenty, IMO. Daggers don't get destroyed by throwing, you should have them on
autopickup (preferably by pickup_exceptions tuned to some #name) to quickly
retrieve them when they're thrown.

Others have said that the lizard corpse belongs in the main inventory, for
several reasons.

